# Each game's own rules at the board: a refused move says why, the
# computer can open when the player takes the second side, and two players
# can form a mill and force a capture, which no computer opponent would
# set up on cue.
expect Board games
tap Reversi
tap Start game
expect Tap a dotted square.
tap-id cell-0
expect That square brackets no opposing discs. Tap a dotted square.
clean
shot reversi-refused
tap-id cell-19
expect The computer placed the marked disc
tap-id game-more
tap Change game
expect Resume Reversi
# Draughts as White against the strongest computer, which opens at once.
tap Draughts
expect Starting replaces your Reversi game in progress.
tap Rules
expect Reach the far side to crown a king.
tap Back
tap White, moves second
tap Strong
tap Start game
expect Your move
expect The computer moved a piece along the marked squares.
clean
shot draughts-second-side
tap-id cell-1
expect That piece has no legal move.
tap-id cell-17
expect Piece selected. Tap a dotted square.
tap-id cell-26
expect Your move
expect-missing Piece selected
tap Moves
expect 1. Computer:
expect 2. You:
tap-id 4294967295
# Between two players: Black offers a man, and White may move only the
# piece that can take it.
tap-id game-more
tap New game
tap Pass-and-play
tap Start game
expect Black to move
tap-id cell-42
tap-id cell-33
expect White to move
tap-id cell-21
tap-id cell-28
tap-id cell-46
tap-id cell-37
expect White to move
tap-id cell-17
expect Captures are mandatory. Select a piece that can capture.
clean
shot draughts-capture-forced
tap-id cell-28
tap-id cell-46
expect Black to move
expect Black 0 · White 0
clean
shot draughts-captured
# Nine Men's Morris with the board held still between two players.
tap-id game-more
tap Change game
tap Nine Men's Morris
expect Place, form mills, move, fly, and remove.
tap Pass-and-play
tap Stays still
tap Start game
expect Placement: tap a dotted point.
tap-id cell-1
expect Tap one of the 24 marked intersections.
tap-id cell-0
expect Pass the reader to White.
expect-missing Board turned
tap-id cell-0
expect Place on an empty marked intersection.
tap-id cell-21
tap-id cell-3
tap-id cell-22
tap-id cell-26
# White completes the bottom row and takes a black piece.
tap-id cell-23
expect Mill formed. Tap a black piece to remove it.
clean
shot morris-mill-white
tap-id cell-26
expect Piece removed.
tap-id cell-45
tap-id cell-25
# Black completes the top row. White's three in a row are protected while
# White has a piece outside a mill.
tap-id cell-6
expect Mill formed. Tap a white piece to remove it.
tap-id cell-21
expect Remove an opposing piece outside a mill, unless every piece is in a mill.
clean
shot morris-protected
tap-id cell-25
expect Piece removed.
expect White to move
tap Moves
expect Black: removed
clean
shot morris-moves
tap-id 4294967295
tap Rules
expect A mill lets you remove one opposing piece.
tap Back
expect White to move
